    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "How to use",
      "pos": [
        780,
        1040
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## H3 Reference Prompter test (no image)\n\nBuilds the same draft the one-per-pose workflow uses, then lets the **H3 Reference Prompter** rewrite it from the pictures. Nothing is drawn: three **Display Text** nodes show the result.\n\n1. Pick a **portrait**, a **costume** and one or more **poses**.\n2. Pick a vision **model** on the H3 Reference Prompter (any `hf:` folder under `models/LLM`).\n3. Queue. Each pose gets its own prompt; the character and outfit are described once.\n\n**Read side by side:**\n- *Draft*: the short prompt from the charsheet.\n- *H3 prompt*: the long prompt. It must keep every `<Picture N>` tag from the draft.\n- *Notes*: what the model saw in each picture. Wrong notes mean a wrong prompt.\n\nThe prompt model is unloaded after the run unless *keep_loaded* is on."
      ]
    }
